1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,230
Hello?

2
00:00:03,230 --> 00:00:04,358
Oh, hello.

3
00:00:04,358 --> 00:00:09,050
I wanted to enquire about hiring a room in the Village Hall,

4
00:00:09,050 --> 00:00:11,800
for the evening of September the first.

5
00:00:11,800 --> 00:00:14,067
Let me just see ...

6
00:00:14,067 --> 00:00:18,600
Yes, we have both rooms available that evening.

7
00:00:18,600 --> 00:00:23,800
There's our Main Hall - that's got seating for 200 people.

8
00:00:23,800 --> 00:00:26,400
Or there's the Charlton Room...

9
00:00:26,400 --> 00:00:27,550
Sorry?

10
00:00:27,550 --> 00:00:34,970
The Charlton Room - C-H-A-R-L-T-O-N.

11
00:00:34,970 --> 00:00:38,150
That's got seating for up to one hundred.

12
00:00:38,150 --> 00:00:43,216
Well, we're organizing a dinner to raise money for a charity,

13
00:00:43,216 --> 00:00:46,900
and we're hoping for at least 150 people,

14
00:00:46,900 --> 00:00:51,188
so I think well go for the Main Hall.

15
00:00:51,188 --> 00:00:53,570
How much would that cost?

16
00:00:53,570 --> 00:00:54,559
Let's see.

17
00:00:54,559 --> 00:00:59,010
You wanted it for the evening of September 1st?

18
00:00:59,010 --> 00:00:59,525
Yes,

19
00:00:59,525 --> 00:01:01,070
that's a Saturday.

20
00:01:01,070 --> 00:01:10,476
So from six pm to midnight that'd be 115 - that's the weekend price,

21
00:01:10,476 --> 00:01:13,370
it's 75 on weekdays.

22
00:01:13,370 --> 00:01:15,000
That's all right.

23
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:21,120
And I have to tell you there's also a deposit of 250,

24
00:01:21,120 --> 00:01:24,850
which is returnable of course as long as there's no damage.

25
00:01:24,850 --> 00:01:30,424
But we do insist that this is paid in cash, we don't take cards

26
00:01:30,424 --> 00:01:31,220
for that.

27
00:01:31,220 --> 00:01:37,345
You can pay the actual rent of the room however you like though -

28
00:01:37,345 --> 00:01:39,230
cash, credit card, cheque ...

29
00:01:39,230 --> 00:01:41,850
Oh, well I suppose thafs OK.

30
00:01:41,850 --> 00:01:47,650
So does the charge include use of tables and chairs and so on?

31
00:01:47,650 --> 00:01:48,750
oh, yes.

32
00:01:48,750 --> 00:01:51,400
And what about parking?

33
00:01:51,400 --> 00:01:51,871
Yeah,

34
00:01:51,871 --> 00:01:53,282
that's all included.

35
00:01:53,282 --> 00:01:59,870
The only thing that isn't included is...you said you were organising a dinner?

36
00:01:59,870 --> 00:02:00,560
Yeah.

37
00:02:00,560 --> 00:02:06,292
Well, you'll have to pay extra for the kitchen if you want to use

38
00:02:06,292 --> 00:02:06,701
that.

39
00:02:06,701 --> 00:02:07,520
It's 25.

40
00:02:07,520 --> 00:02:13,220
It's got very good facilities - good quality cookers and fridges and so on.

41
00:02:13,220 --> 00:02:16,415
OK, well I suppose that s all right.

42
00:02:16,415 --> 00:02:20,010
We can cover the cost in our entry charges.

43
00:02:20,010 --> 00:02:20,392
Right.

44
00:02:20,392 --> 00:02:23,070
So I'll make a note of that.

45
00:02:23,070 --> 00:02:28,652
Now there are just one or two things you need to think about before

46
00:02:28,652 --> 00:02:29,450
the event.

47
00:02:29,450 --> 00:02:34,497
For example, you'll have to see about getting a licence if you're planning to

48
00:02:34,497 --> 00:02:36,660
have any music during the meal.

49
00:02:36,660 --> 00:02:37,720
Oh, really?

50
00:02:37,720 --> 00:02:41,950
it's quite straightforward, I'll give you the details later on.

51
00:02:41,950 --> 00:02:47,944
And about a week or ten days before your event you'll need to contact

52
00:02:47,944 --> 00:02:48,800
the caretaker,

53
00:02:48,800 --> 00:02:55,000
that's Mr Evans, to make the arrangements for entry-he'll sort that out with you.

54
00:02:55,000 --> 00:02:58,100
And do I give him the payment as well?

55
00:02:58,100 --> 00:03:00,850
No, you do that directly with me.

56
00:03:00,850 --> 00:03:01,487
Right.

57
00:03:01,487 --> 00:03:10,400
Now is there anything I need to know about what happens during the event?

58
00:03:10,400 --> 00:03:16,090
Well, as you'll be aware, of course the building is no smoking throughout.

59
00:03:16,090 --> 00:03:17,170
Of course.

60
00:03:17,170 --> 00:03:19,280
Now, are you having a band?

61
00:03:19,280 --> 00:03:20,510
Yes.

62
00:03:20,510 --> 00:03:22,920
Well, they'll have a lot of equipment,

63
00:03:22,920 --> 00:03:28,263
so rather than using the front door they should park their van round the back

64
00:03:28,263 --> 00:03:30,400
and use the stage door there.

65
00:03:30,400 --> 00:03:35,001
You can open that from inside but don't forget to lock it at the

66
00:03:35,001 --> 00:03:35,330
end.

67
00:03:35,330 --> 00:03:36,370
OK.

68
00:03:36,370 --> 00:03:40,710
And talking of bands, I'm sure I don't need to tell you this,

69
00:03:40,710 --> 00:03:45,556
but you must make sure that no one fiddles about with the black box

70
00:03:45,556 --> 00:03:46,940
by the fire door

71
00:03:46,940 --> 00:03:52,392
that's a system that cuts in when the volume reaches a certain level.

72
00:03:52,392 --> 00:03:54,070
It's a legal requirement.

73
00:03:54,070 --> 00:03:54,419
Sure.

74
00:03:54,419 --> 00:03:58,607
Anyway, we want people to be able to talk to one another

75
00:03:58,607 --> 00:04:01,050
so we don't want anything too loud.

76
00:04:01,050 --> 00:04:01,614
Oh,

77
00:04:01,614 --> 00:04:08,380
that reminds me, we'll be having speeches - are there any microphones available?

78
00:04:08,380 --> 00:04:08,761
Yeah.

79
00:04:08,761 --> 00:04:12,570
Just let the caretaker know, he'll get those for you.

80
00:04:12,570 --> 00:04:18,123
Right, now when the event is over we do ask that the premises are

81
00:04:18,123 --> 00:04:19,710
left in good condition.

82
00:04:19,710 --> 00:04:25,096
So there's a locked cupboard and you'll be informed of the code you need

83
00:04:25,096 --> 00:04:26,250
to open that.

84
00:04:26,250 --> 00:04:32,000
It's got all the cleaning equipment, brushes and detergent and so on.

85
00:04:32,000 --> 00:04:32,465
Right.

86
00:04:32,465 --> 00:04:37,115
So what do we need to do after everyone's gone?

87
00:04:37,115 --> 00:04:39,440
Sweep the floors I suppose?

88
00:04:39,440 --> 00:04:43,700
Well, actually they have to be washed, not just swept.

89
00:04:43,700 --> 00:04:48,010
Then you'll be provided with black plastic bags,

90
00:04:48,010 --> 00:04:52,200
so all the rubbish must be collected up and left outside the door.

91
00:04:52,200 --> 00:04:53,175
Of course.

92
00:04:53,175 --> 00:04:56,100
We'll make sure everything's left tidy.

93
00:04:56,100 --> 00:04:56,516
Oh,

94
00:04:56,516 --> 00:05:02,340
and I forgot to ask, I presume we can have decorations in the room?

95
00:05:02,340 --> 00:05:02,775
Yes,

96
00:05:02,775 --> 00:05:05,820
but you must take them down afterwards.

97
00:05:05,820 --> 00:05:06,720
Sure.

98
00:05:06,720 --> 00:05:11,568
And the chairs and tables should be stacked up neatly at the back of

99
00:05:11,568 --> 00:05:12,260
the room.

100
00:05:12,260 --> 00:05:17,000
I'll make sure I've got a few people to help me.
